TIP:  It’s important to get the strumming pattern down to emulate Iz’s ukulele.  For the intro it’s a downstroke at the beginning of each chord change and then 8th notes, so D DUDUDU.  For the verse it’s either this same pattern or a backed off D DUD DU.  

TIP:  It’s subtle, but the second (Em) chord in the intro is an (Em7) so hold form and add your pinky to note <d> on the 2nd string/3rd fret.  If you want to keep it simple, just play another (Em).

TIP:  To play the (A7sus4) from the (Am7) just hold form and add your pinky to the 2nd string/3rd fret note <d>.  To simplify this bit, just play another (Am7) and hold through to the (D).  


